---
// Abstract / motivation section.
---
<section id="abstract" class="content-section">
  <div class="section-container">
    <h2 class="section-title">Abstract</h2>

    <p class="lead">
      Foundation-model agents now run in search, browsing, coding, and embodied settings, where quality
      hinges on <strong>long-horizon interaction</strong>: small errors compound across tool calls and memory,
      and single-turn evaluation misses them. This tutorial gives an operational view of agent failure modes,
      how to <strong>trigger</strong> them reproducibly, <strong>diagnose</strong> them from traces, and
      <strong>verify</strong> that fixes hold.
    </p>

    <div class="learn-grid">
      <div class="learn-card">
        <div class="learn-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><path d="M12 6v6l4 2"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Long-horizon failures, made concrete</h3>
        <p>
          Error cascades, brittle tool use, unstable memory, reward hacking, and diversity collapse,
          each grounded in a minimal reproduction.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="learn-card">
        <div class="learn-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M3 3v18h18"/><path d="M7 14l3-3 4 4 5-6"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Trace-level diagnostics</h3>
        <p>
          Reward variance, policy entropy, gradient-norm spikes, and trace logs as early
          indicators of collapse and reward hacking.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="learn-card">
        <div class="learn-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10z"/><path d="M9 12l2 2 4-4"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>Verified fixes, not just patches</h3>
        <p>
          Reward and constraint design, trajectory filtering, KL choices, and recovery mechanisms,
          evaluated against negative baselines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="learn-card">
        <div class="learn-icon" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
            <path d="M20.59 13.41l-7.17 7.17a2 2 0 0 1-2.83 0L2 12V2h10l8.59 8.59a2 2 0 0 1 0 2.82z"/>
            <line x1="7" y1="7" x2="7.01" y2="7"/>
          </svg>
        </div>
        <h3>A shared protocol</h3>
        <p>
          Shared conventions for naming failures, logging traces, and writing reproductions
          so results transfer across papers.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h3 class="subsection-title">Audience and prerequisites</h3>
    <p class="lead">
      For NLP researchers and practitioners interested in agentic AI. We assume basic probability,
      calculus, and machine learning (including REINFORCE-level RL); LLM prompting experience helps
      but is not required.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  #abstract { background: white; padding: 4rem 1rem; }
  .section-container { max-width: var(--page-max-width, 1100px); margin: 0 auto; }
  .section-title {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #2a2f6c;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #444;
    margin: 0 auto 1.2rem;
    max-width: 820px;
  }

  .lead strong { color: #2a2f6c; font-weight: 600; }

  .learn-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.2rem;
    margin: 2.5rem auto 0;
    max-width: 1000px;
  }

  .learn-card {
    background: #f8f9fb;
    border: 1px solid #e9ecf3;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 1.4rem 1.4rem;
    transition: transform 0.2s ease, box-shadow 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;
  }

  .learn-card:hover {
    transform: translateY(-2px);
    box-shadow: 0 10px 24px rgba(42, 47, 108, 0.07);
    border-color: rgba(42, 47, 108, 0.18);
  }

  .learn-icon {
    width: 38px;
    height: 38px;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 10px;
    background: rgba(42, 47, 108, 0.1);
    color: #2a2f6c;
    margin-bottom: 0.8rem;
  }

  .learn-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    color: #2a2f6c;
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .learn-card p {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.65;
  }

  .subsection-title {
    font-size: 1.3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #333;
    margin: 3rem auto 0.7rem;
    max-width: 820px;
    border-left: 3px solid #2a2f6c;
    padding-left: 0.7rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .learn-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .section-title { font-size: 1.9rem; }
  }
</style>
